@vsm 1.0
// omega_calibration_coverage.spec.vsm
// Author: Claude [O], 2026-07-24. Status: SEED (design). Ref: ds_queue q15.
// Gate lifted: [O] writes this before [S] runs.

spec(OMEGA-CALIBRATION-COVERAGE) {

  problem: "~half the s1-clima L3 network cannot classify its own viability. At a
            hourly tick, 51 of 87 nodes emit 'Ω not calibrated — raw state emitted'
            instead of IN/OUT Ω. A node without Ω has no envelope to be inside or
            outside of — it reports raw state but cannot say whether that state is
            viable. The excursion-tracking primitive (memory) is inert on those nodes."

  not_a_regression: "Pre-existing, not caused by the Stage 3 rollout. Memory records
                     '12/12 Ω calibrada' when the network had 12 nodes (2026-06-26).
                     It grew to 87; calibration did not follow. Ω is built per-node from
                     EXTERNAL data (ERA5 reanalysis) by omega_calibrate.py, so each new
                     node needs its own fetch+build — that step never scaled with the
                     node count."

  measured_2026_07_24: "87 L3 units. 43 omega json files in /var/lib/vsf-clima/omega/.
                        BUT runtime showed only 36 calibrated at the tick. The three
                        numbers disagree, and the gap is the first thing to resolve —
                        file-exists != loads-successfully != node-actually-uses-it."

  // ── THE DIAGNOSIS MUST COME FIRST (confirm-first; do not mass-recalibrate blind) ──
  phase_0_diagnose: "Before generating ANY new Ω, resolve the 87 / 43 / 36 discrepancy.
                     For each of the 87 node-ids, classify into exactly one bucket:
                       (a) NO FILE           — omega/<node_id>.json absent → needs build
                       (b) FILE, LOADS, USED — calibrated and working (the 36)
                       (c) FILE BUT UNUSED   — file exists yet node still emits 'not
                                               calibrated' → load_omega() fails OR the
                                               filename node-id != the node's --node-id.
                                               THIS is a bug to fix, not a recalibration.
                     Bucket (c) is the likely 43-vs-36 gap (7 files that exist but don't
                     load/match). Fixing (c) is free coverage — no ERA5 fetch needed."

  phase_1_build: "For bucket (a) only: run omega_calibrate.py per missing node. It
                  fetches ERA5 (lat/lon per node registry) and writes omega/<id>.json.
                  This touches EXTERNAL data — respect feedback_data_provenance_boundary:
                  ERA5 history for the baseline is fine (input); do NOT let any external
                  FORECAST become an output. Ω is a baseline envelope, not a prediction."

  fierro_gate: "omega_calibrate.py already applies the Fierro Q1 fix (log1p transform,
                line 137). Any newly-built Ω must still pass the Fierro Q1-Q3 domain
                protocol (memory project_fierro_protocol): Q1 Ω convex, Q2 L<1, Q3
                σ_max bounded. A node whose data yields a non-convex or degenerate Ω is
                a FINDING (report it), not a node to force-calibrate with a bad envelope —
                a wrong Ω is worse than an honest 'not calibrated'."

  acceptance: "At a tick after the work: count nodes emitting IN/OUT Ω vs 'not
               calibrated' with probe.sh-style measurement (match the STRUCTURAL token,
               not one phrasing — the mistake that read 51 healthy nodes as mute today).
               Target: bucket (c) → 0 (bug fixed), bucket (a) → built or explicitly
               deferred-with-reason. Every remaining 'not calibrated' node must have a
               named reason (no ERA5 coverage / failed Fierro gate), not silence."

  owner: "[O] design (this spec) · [S] phase_0 diagnose + phase_1 build. Not a nucleus
          change, not a signal-path change — safe for [S] once phase_0 is reported."
}
